{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "04E2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\tau = fppf$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$I$", "MATH_0004": "$A/I \\to \\overline{B}$", "MATH_0005": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0006": "$B/IB \\not = 0$", "MATH_0007": "$A/I \\to B/IB$", "MATH_0008": "$\\overline{B}$", "MATH_0009": "$f_{big, *} : \\textit{Ab}((\\Sch/X)_{fppf})\n\\to \\textit{Ab}((\\Sch/Y)_{fppf})$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-closed-immersion-pushforward-exact}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-closed-immersion-almost-cocontinuous}", "TEXTCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTOPEN_0001": "\\href{mailto:stacks.project@gmail.com}{"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-fppf-closed-immersion-not-closed}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0a454123d9af27e555f3028f70a8b9182017a15ebb11503449736b9d6138069a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:01344959257f90e906c5981bb210c7d0ce5680db29d65741e833e7bf4e331fb2", "source_text": "In Lemma <REF_0001> the case <MATH_0001>\nis missing. The reason is that given a ring <MATH_0002>, an ideal <MATH_0003> and a\nfaithfully flat, finitely presented ring map <MATH_0004>, there\nis no reason to think that one can find <TEXTITOPEN_0001>any<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> flat finitely presented ring\nmap <MATH_0005> with <MATH_0006> such that <MATH_0007> factors through\n<MATH_0008>. Hence the proof of\nLemma <REF_0002>\ndoes not work for the fppf topology.\nIn fact it is likely false that\n<MATH_0009>\nis exact when <MATH_0010> is a closed immersion.\nIf you know an example, please email\n<TEXTOPEN_0001>stacks.project@gmail.com<TEXTCLOSE_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bbf1a1f16077ff20c0279f69f01da551ab097e8985a17401f96633727671ab86", "unit_id": "tag:04C5:statement"}
